From 447d9ac51d67f2b5463a58591409bf3ef5d8ae7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claud McClaudeson <claud@pantsforbirds.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 05:08:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] sw DOCX: widow and orphan control in split table rows,
 like Word 2013

Word 2013+ (DOCX compatibilityMode 15) applies widow and orphan control
to paragraphs in table rows split across pages: a 4-line paragraph with
room for 3 lines is split 2+2. Word <= 2010 doesn't, and splits it 3+1.

Writer only did this in floating tables. Do it in all tables for Word
2013+ documents (TABLE_ROW_KEEP without ADD_FLY_OFFSETS).

Change-Id: I45125a6aea213eeb2feea3d7ebb1d2a90b5a5316
